,"source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":16,"level":7,"moves":[33,189]},{"species":17,"level":9,"moves":[33,189,16]}]},{"id":"bugsy","title":"Bugsy","where":"Azalea Town Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":1,"recommended":16,"tips":"Bug team. Scyther's Fury Cutter gets stronger every turn, so take it out fast. Fire, Flying and Rock moves are the answers; Thundershock helps against Scyther too.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":11,"level":14,"moves":[33,81,106]},{"species":14,"level":14,"moves":[40,81,106]},{"species":123,"level":16,"moves":[98,43,210]}]},{"id":"whitney","title":"Whitney","where":"Goldenrod City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":2,"recommended":20,"tips":"Miltank is the wall of the early game: Rollout, Attract and Milk Drink. Fighting moves are the clean answer (Machop, Mankey). A Pokémon that resists Rollout helps; Attract can stop a male starter, so bring a spare.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":35,"level":18,"moves":[3,102,227,118]},{"species":241,"level":20,"moves":[205,213,23,208]}]},{"id":"morty","title":"Morty","where":"Ecruteak City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":3,"recommended":25,"tips":"Ghost team. Normal and Fighting moves cannot touch Ghosts. Psychic, Dark and Ground moves work, and Flying types like Noctowl or Togetic handle the Poison half well.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":92,"level":21,"moves":[122,180,212,174]},{"species":93,"level":21,"moves":[95,102,174,101]},{"species":94,"level":25,"moves":[95,247,212,138]},{"species":93,"level":23,"moves":[180,212,102,101]}]},{"id":"chuck","title":"Chuck","where":"Cianwood City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":5,"recommended":30,"tips":"Fighting team. Psychic, Flying and Ghost types do well; Xatu is a strong pick. Poliwrath's DynamicPunch always confuses, so keep a Pokémon in reserve.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":57,"level":27,"moves":[43,99,2,154]},{"species":62,"level":30,"moves":[95,170,57,223]}]},{"id":"jasmine","title":"Jasmine","where":"Olivine City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":4,"recommended":35,"tips":"Steel team: two Magnemite and a Steelix. Fire and Fighting moves are the answer; Ground also works on Magnemite. Heal Amphy at the lighthouse first (Secret Potion from Cianwood) or she will not battle you.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":81,"level":30,"moves":[85,48,49,86]},{"species":81,"level":30,"moves":[85,48,49,86]},{"species":208,"level":35,"moves":[103,241,88,231]}]},{"id":"pryce","title":"Pryce","where":"Mahogany Town Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":6,"recommended":31,"tips":"Ice team. Fire, Fighting and Rock moves are best. Dewgong and Piloswine use Rest, so attack while they sleep and keep Full Heals for Frozen Pokémon.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":86,"level":27,"moves":[29,196,62,156]},{"species":87,"level":29,"moves":[29,196,62,156]},{"species":221,"level":31,"moves":[196,31,54,59]}]},{"id":"clair","title":"Clair","where":"Blackthorn City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"johto","badge":7,"recommended":40,"tips":"Three Dragonair and a Kingdra. Ice and Electric moves are the answers; Kingdra is only weak to Dragon. Piloswine and Lanturn are good partners.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":148,"level":37,"moves":[86,57,21,225]},{"species":148,"level":37,"moves":[86,85,21,225]},{"species":148,"level":37,"moves":[86,58,21,225]},{"species":230,"level":40,"moves":[108,57,63,225]}]},{"id":"will","title":"Will","where":"Indigo Plateau (Elite Four 1)","kind":"e4","region":"johto","badge":-1,"recommended":42,"tips":"Psychic team. Dark types are the cleanest answer (Umbreon, Houndoom); Ampharos also helps. Jynx, Slowbro and Xatu are the main threats.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/elite-four","mons":[{"species":178,"level":40,"moves":[98,248,109,94]},{"species":124,"level":41,"moves":[3,142,8,94]},{"species":103,"level":41,"moves":[115,73,121,94]},{"species":80,"level":41,"moves":[174,133,34,94]},{"species":178,"level":42,"moves":[98,248,109,94]}],"flag":1464},{"id":"koga","title":"Koga","where":"Indigo Plateau (Elite Four 2)","kind":"e4","region":"johto","badge":-1,"recommended":44,"tips":"Poison/Bug team (Koga is Elite Four in this game). Psychic and Fire answer most of it. Crobat, Muk and Forretress are the threats.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/elite-four","mons":[{"species":168,"level":40,"moves":[104,169,226,202]},{"species":49,"level":41,"moves":[48,16,94,92]},{"species":205,"level":43,"moves":[182,129,153,191]},{"species":89,"level":42,"moves":[107,151,188,92]},{"species":169,"level":44,"moves":[104,98,17,92]}],"flag":1465},{"id":"bruno","title":"Bruno","where":"Indigo Plateau (Elite Four 3)","kind":"e4","region":"johto","badge":-1,"recommended":46,"tips":"Fighting team plus Onix. Psychic and Flying support work well; handle Onix separately with Water or Grass moves. Machamp and Hitmonlee hit hardest.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/elite-four","mons":[{"species":237,"level":42,"moves":[228,98,91,197]},{"species":106,"level":42,"moves":[207,24,136,193]},{"species":107,"level":42,"moves":[9,8,7,183]},{"species":95,"level":43,"moves":[20,89,201,157]},{"species":68,"level":46,"moves":[157,193,233,238]}],"flag":1466},{"id":"karen","title":"Karen","where":"Indigo Plateau (Elite Four 4)","kind":"e4","region":"johto","badge":-1,"recommended":47,"tips":"Dark team. Do not rely only on Psychic coverage: Fighting, Bug and Water moves help. Houndoom, Umbreon and Gengar are the threats.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/elite-four","mons":[{"species":197,"level":42,"moves":[28,109,185,212]},{"species":45,"level":42,"moves":[78,51,236,80]},{"species":94,"level":45,"moves":[122,180,174,194]},{"species":198,"level":44,"moves":[98,18,228,185]},{"species":229,"level":47,"moves":[46,228,53,242]}],"flag":1467},{"id":"lance","title":"Lance","where":"Indigo Plateau (Champion)","kind":"champion","region":"johto","badge":-1,"recommended":50,"tips":"Dragon team. Ice coverage is the cleanest answer to several Dragonite; Electric helps against Gyarados. Lapras, Jynx, Ampharos and Piloswine are good picks.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/elite-four","mons":[{"species":130,"level":44,"moves":[175,240,57,63]},{"species":149,"level":47,"moves":[86,239,87,63]},{"species":149,"level":47,"moves":[86,239,59,63]},{"species":142,"level":46,"moves":[17,246,157,63]},{"species":6,"level":46,"moves":[53,17,163,63]},{"species":149,"level":50,"moves":[126,219,200,63]}],"flag":1468},{"id":"surge","title":"Lt. Surge","where":"Vermilion City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":2,"recommended":46,"tips":"Electric team. Ground moves are the answer (Nidoking, Steelix, Rhydon). The trash-can switches open the door to him.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":26,"level":44,"moves":[86,98,85,87]},{"species":101,"level":40,"moves":[103,104,129,153]},{"species":82,"level":40,"moves":[199,104,129,192]},{"species":101,"level":40,"moves":[103,104,129,153]},{"species":125,"level":46,"moves":[98,9,113,87]}]},{"id":"sabrina","title":"Sabrina","where":"Saffron City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":5,"recommended":48,"tips":"Psychic team. Dark moves and Ghost moves are effective and she has no real answer to them. Walk the teleporter maze to reach her.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":196,"level":46,"moves":[28,98,129,94]},{"species":122,"level":46,"moves":[112,115,226,94]},{"species":65,"level":48,"moves":[105,248,94,115]}]},{"id":"erika","title":"Erika","where":"Celadon City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":3,"recommended":46,"tips":"Grass team that leans on status moves. Fire, Flying and Ice moves are best; bring Full Restores or status healers. Sunny Day boosts your Fire moves.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":114,"level":42,"moves":[22,20,202,79]},{"species":189,"level":41,"moves":[72,73,178,202]},{"species":71,"level":46,"moves":[241,235,51,75]},{"species":182,"level":46,"moves":[241,235,80,76]}]},{"id":"janine","title":"Janine","where":"Fuchsia City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":4,"recommended":39,"tips":"Poison team. Psychic and Ground moves work well. She hides among look-alike trainers, so check the gym guide for the real one.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":169,"level":36,"moves":[103,48,109,17]},{"species":110,"level":36,"moves":[123,188,92,153]},{"species":110,"level":36,"moves":[123,188,92,153]},{"species":168,"level":33,"moves":[184,202,81,101]},{"species":49,"level":39,"moves":[193,104,16,94]}]},{"id":"misty","title":"Misty","where":"Cerulean City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":1,"recommended":47,"tips":"Water team. Grass and Electric moves are the answers (Meganium, Ampharos, Raichu). Lapras and Starmie carry Ice moves.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":55,"level":42,"moves":[57,50,244,94]},{"species":195,"level":42,"moves":[57,133,89,240]},{"species":131,"level":44,"moves":[57,195,59,240]},{"species":121,"level":47,"moves":[57,109,105,58]}]},{"id":"brock","title":"Brock","where":"Pewter City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":0,"recommended":44,"tips":"Rock team. Grass, Water and Fighting moves are strong; Meganium is a great fit. Electric moves help against Omastar and Kabutops.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":75,"level":41,"moves":[111,157,205,89]},{"species":111,"level":41,"moves":[31,184,89,32]},{"species":139,"level":42,"moves":[44,57,182,131]},{"species":95,"level":44,"moves":[20,157,117,201]},{"species":141,"level":42,"moves":[163,57,203,202]}]},{"id":"blaine","title":"Blaine","where":"Seafoam Islands Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":6,"recommended":50,"tips":"Fire team. Water moves are best, with Rock and Ground as backup. Bring a Burn Heal.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":219,"level":45,"moves":[174,123,53,157]},{"species":126,"level":45,"moves":[9,7,241,109]},{"species":78,"level":50,"moves":[98,83,31,126]}]},{"id":"blue","title":"Blue","where":"Viridian City Gym","kind":"gym","region":"kanto","badge":7,"recommended":58,"tips":"Mixed team (the Kanto finale). Bring Electric, Ice, Rock and Water answers; he has no single weakness to exploit, so use several Pokémon.","source":"https://www.serebii.net/gs/gyms.shtml","mons":[{"species":18,"level":56,"moves":[98,18,17,119]},{"species":65,"level":54,"moves":[50,105,94,115]},{"species":112,"level":56,"moves":[31,201,157,89]},{"species":130,"level":58,"moves":[239,56,240,63]},{"species":103,"level":58,"moves":[241,73,121,76]},{"species":59,"level":58,"moves":[46,129,53,245]}]},{"id":"red","title":"Red","where":"Mt. Silver summit","kind":"red","region":"kanto","badge":-1,"recommended":65,"tips":"Six strong Pokémon across Electric, Psychic, Normal, Grass, Fire and Water. A level 60-70+ team is the usual target. Ground handles Pikachu, keep a dedicated plan for Snorlax, and carry lots of healing.","source":"https://nationaldex.io/guide/pokemon-gold-silver-crystal/red-battle","mons":[{"species":25,"level":81,"moves":[204,98,85,87]},{"species":196,"level":73,"moves":[189,115,129,94]},{"species":143,"level":75,"moves":[133,173,156,34]},{"species":3,"level":77,"moves":[241,202,235,76]},{"species":6,"level":77,"moves":[53,17,163,83]},{"species":9,"level":77,"moves":[240,57,59,250]}],"flag":1890}]}